    "body": "### Issue type\n\nDocumentation Bug\n\n### Have you reproduced the bug with TensorFlow Nightly?\n\nNo\n\n### Source\n\nsource\n\n### TensorFlow version\n\n2.17.0\n\n### Custom code\n\nYes\n\n### OS platform and distribution\n\nUbuntu 24.04.3 LTS\n\n### Mobile device\n\n_No response_\n\n### Python version\n\n3.10.19\n\n### Bazel version\n\n_No response_\n\n### GCC/compiler version\n\n_No response_\n\n### CUDA/cuDNN version\n\nCUDA: 12.3, cuDNN: 8\n\n### GPU model and memory\n\n4 × NVIDIA RTX 3090 (24GB each)\n\n### Current behavior?\n\n- TensorFlow guide(s) state that layers/models can track metrics via `add_metric()` (often used inside `call()` in subclassed models).\n- On TF 2.17.0 + Keras 3.4.1 (TF backend), using `self.add_metric(...)` inside `call()` is not a reliable supported pattern. This aligns with existing reports where `add_metric` is “permanently disabled” in the codepath.\n- As a result, the docs example/messaging is misleading for Keras 3 users.\n\n**Expected behavior**\n- TensorFlow docs should be updated to not recommend `add_metric()` inside `call()` for Keras 3.\n- Docs should show the Keras 3-compatible approach (create a `keras.metrics.Metric` object in `__init__`, call update_state, expose via metrics property, or use a custom `train_step`).\n\n### Standalone code to reproduce the issue\n\n```shell\nimport os\nos.environ[\"KERAS_BACKEND\"] = \"tensorflow\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport tensorflow as tf\nimport keras\n\nprint(\"TF:\", tf.__version__)\nprint(\"Keras:\", keras.__version__)\nprint(\"Backend:\", keras.backend.backend())\n\nclass M(keras.Model):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.d = keras.layers.Dense(4)\n\n    def call(self, x):\n        y = self.d(x)\n        m = keras.losses.MeanSquaredError()(x, y)\n        # This is the pattern implied by TF guides (\"track metrics via add_metric\")\n        self.add_metric(m, name=\"reconstruction_loss\")\n        return y\n\nx = np.random.randn(8, 4).astype(\"float32\")\nm = M()\n\n# Force eager + disable jit to avoid GPU/XLA changing warning surfaces\nm.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"mse\", run_eagerly=True, jit_compile=False)\n\ntry:\n    hist = m.fit(x, x, epochs=1, verbose=0)\n    print(\"history keys:\", sorted(list(hist.history.keys())))\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"EXCEPTION:\", type(e).__name__, str(e))\n\nprint(\"metrics:\", [mm.name for mm in m.metrics])\n```\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n2026-02-23 00:24:36.838904: E external/local_xla/xla/stream_executor/cuda/cuda_fft.cc:485] Unable to register cuFFT factory: Attempting to register factory for plugin cuFFT when one has already been registered\n2026-02-23 00:24:36.859605: E external/local_xla/xla/stream_executor/cuda/cuda_dnn.cc:8454] Unable to register cuDNN factory: Attempting to register factory for plugin cuDNN when one has already been registered\n2026-02-23 00:24:36.865974: E external/local_xla/xla/stream_executor/cuda/cuda_blas.cc:1452] Unable to register cuBLAS factory: Attempting to register factory for plugin cuBLAS when one has already been registered\n```",
